are down regulated in a rat model of cholestasis</article-title><source>J Hepatol</source><year>1992</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>220</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1324272</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0168-8278(92)90040-V</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bergasa</surname><given-names>NV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The pruritus of cholestasis</article-title><source>J Hepatol</source><year>2005</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>1078</fpage><lpage>1088</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16253381</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lugo</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kern</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The pharmacokinetics of oxycodone</article-title><source>Journal of Pain and Palliative Care Pharmacotherapy</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15760805</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1300/J354v18n04_03</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naranjo</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Busto</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Sellers</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandor</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruiz</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Janecek</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Domecq</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenblatt</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A method for estimating the probability of adverse drug reactions</article-title><source>Clin Pharmacol Ther</source><year>1981</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7249508</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Danan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000e9;nichou</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Causality assessment of adverse reactions to drugs. I. A novel method based on the conclusions of international consensus meetings: application to drug-induced liver injuries</article-title><source>J Clin Epidemiol</source><year>1993</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>1323</fpage><lpage>1330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8229110</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0895-4356(93)90101-6</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>